Z||000026||Ken Wittlief||06-13-2001||10:07 AM||||I think about 45% of suicide bombers end up blowing themselves up in their own basement or garage.<P>  If you really think about it, its disturbing. We look down on people that do stuff like this, and we cant understand the Japanese Kamakazie pilots that did this in WW2.<P>  but the american and british bomber crews that flew over germany had horrendous casualty rates - their chances of surviving 10 consecutive missions were near zero.<P>  so in effect, werent they pretty much on suicide missions too?<P>  and the infintry in WW2, they pretty much had to resign themselves to the fact that they had a very high likelyhood of being killed in action.<P>  So if you are going out to kill people, and the odds are you will die in the process, where do you draw the line between the suicide bombers and the rest of the military?<P>   When it gets to the point where humans are killing each other, logic and reasoning is lost.<p>[This message has been edited by Ken Wittlief (edited 06-13-2001).]||||reg||1
